7. Strings :

String s = "hello";

System.out.println(s.length()); //5
system.out.println(s.charAt(1));  //e
system.out.println(s.substring(1,4)) //ell
System.out.println(s.equals("hi")); // false
System.out.println(s.compareTo("hi")); //lexicographic compare

Strings are immutable ( cannot be directly changed )
Use StringBuilder for fast modifications :
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("abc");
sb.append("d"); // "abcd"
sb.reverse();  // "dcba"


